  "lineage": "Trinidad Orisha worship, formerly called Shango, is an African-derived religion of Yoruba origin whose annual feasts at shrines feature songs to the orishas in a Yoruba-derived liturgical language, raised by a lead singer and answered by the congregation. A battery of three drums with shac-shac rattles accompanies the songs and the spirit possession they invite; George Eaton Simpson recorded the music for Folkways. The membrane-drum card stands in for the three drums.",
